trying to envision what the economy looked like 100 years ago you you would have a hard time really understanding what a large portion of what our jobs looks like Yeah exactly what you what you just suggeste", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2091252532689658001#t=1056", "end": 1175.919, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "7bb4936025e909af4d5326d259f575b4adbb77bb4cf65dd6a30235ad8f48f066", "start": 1056.082, "text": "So, I thi- this is a really interesting question I think there are sort of two competing forces On the one hand you, have access to incredible scope with AI I don't know anything about building a website but Claude does I do know what maybe", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2091252532689658001#t=1290", "end": 1410.22, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "e3adf34fe4416181e2908b6701e0cb9f9e1b72bd6fda48f830d0f96b38a70cc1", "start": 1290.488, "text": "in otherwise standard macroeconomic models you can generate things that look like infinite growth and finite time and I think understanding that dimension of let's say like the economic singularity or the prospect of the economic singularit", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2091252532689658001#t=0", "end": 81.979, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "4d35e5d13079006f48784ece173c41b746dd781db29bb78c2fb79e4614dbd744", "start": 0.08, "text": "I think about my job as an economist Yes, Claude is increasingly able to download data, run regressions, even build economic models And, you know, six months ago I might have thought to myself well I still have this comparative advantage at", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2091252532689658001#t=139", "end": 256.672, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "exc