{"card_hash": "17023b63651467ce9bdc1d22a5f1c8d7619a8254fb2b6f972e16074252084fc1", "channel": "matt palmer", "chars": 30458, "chars_all_clips": 30458, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 16, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=0", "end": 119.066, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "570d35be0edbcd17a23716aca9037599d1442c12d2e63746d75ba0356dd4e859", "start": 0.12, "text": "Hey Grokbot could you go get that information off of Twitter for each of my followers either through the API or by physically going and looking at their profile create a Notion database pull that information into the database and then hand ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=447", "end": 565.431, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "607d05a7983cc11c63cc26593f700d647a3a54926775c27be46836a9db9d281d", "start": 447.526, "text": "approved the build From there, it actually started a build in Cursor which if we take a look at Cursor Cloud in Chrome we see that the build is running And this is the really nice part about the integration with Cursor which is that if you ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=733", "end": 852.283, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "989c1433beb43b739d8a8ae99b419cbee370baab6ee664c3356adfc5d3fcb8f8", "start": 733.243, "text": "to those two sites because I logged in with them So I mentioned that bots can be run in three different ways. And those are first, if you send a bot a message Second if you define a routine or a trigger that kicks off the bot But third, bot", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=852", "end": 971.497, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "51cf8b42ee386a70876fb0276f04b0d0968d295ab19e8303b02785a45ca700ae", "start": 852.303, "text": "different ideas and it presents an opportunity for you to come up with some amazing ideas and share them with everyone So we can actually see here that the cursor product expert shared a change log from earlier today and now it's passing it", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=1063", "end": 1180.583, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "dbf2ae216bf7b7d4fcde88a218b469a73fc764a32d196df35285f3368e42a981", "start": 1063.551, "text": "I'm the annoying coffee guy out here asking people to grab a coffee This, I mean, quite literally, I spun up in 15 minutes actually I think closer to 10 minutes with my phone this morning And that means it's less about what you can build an", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=1420", "end": 1540.293, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "38230311ac17b3820afced9856220d349c785ce52c53aa040f080a2b3478bda1", "start": 1420.53, "text": "Basically what we want is some outer loop where we're gathering context understanding problems pulling in context from these different systems before we kick it off to a cloud agent that acts as our inner loop and actually builds the softwa", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Productivity and Workflows", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=0", "end": 119.066, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "570d35be0edbcd17a23716aca9037599d1442c12d2e63746d75ba0356dd4e859", "start": 0.12, "text": "Hey Grokbot could you go get that information off of Twitter for each of my followers either through the API or by physically going and looking at their profile create a Notion database pull that information into the database and then hand ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=447", "end": 565.431, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "607d05a7983cc11c63cc26593f700d647a3a54926775c27be46836a9db9d281d", "start": 447.526, "text": "approved the build From there, it actually started a build in Cursor which if we take a look at Cursor Cloud in Chrome we see that the build is running And this is the really nice part about the integration with Cursor which is that if you ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=733", "end": 852.283, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "989c1433beb43b739d8a8ae99b419cbee370baab6ee664c3356adfc5d3fcb8f8", "start": 733.243, "text": "to those two sites because I logged in with them So I mentioned that bots can be run in three different ways. And those are first, if you send a bot a message Second if you define a routine or a trigger that kicks off the bot But third, bot", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=852", "end": 971.497, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "51cf8b42ee386a70876fb0276f04b0d0968d295ab19e8303b02785a45ca700ae", "start": 852.303, "text": "different ideas and it presents an opportunity for you to come up with some amazing ideas and share them with everyone So we can actually see here that the cursor product expert shared a change log from earlier today and now it's passing it", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=1063", "end": 1180.583, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "dbf2ae216bf7b7d4fcde88a218b469a73fc764a32d196df35285f3368e42a981", "start": 1063.551, "text": "I'm the annoying coffee guy out here asking people to grab a coffee This, I mean, quite literally, I spun up in 15 minutes actually I think closer to 10 minutes with my phone this morning And that means it's less about what you can build an", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681#t=1420", "end": 1540.293, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "38230311ac17b3820afced9856220d349c785ce52c53aa040f080a2b3478bda1", "start": 1420.53, "text": "Basically what we want is some outer loop where we're gathering context understanding problems pulling in context from these different systems before we kick it off to a cloud agent that acts as our inner loop and actually builds the softwa", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "hint": null, "platform": "x", "profile": "librarian", "schema_version": 1, "selection_version": "spread-longest-v1", "slug": "matt_palmer_-_Getting_Started_with_Grok_Bot_01_00_What_is_Bot_05_26_Anatomy_of_a", "source_revision": "2f05c77ccdbb5c062ba4f98498553bf69f612ae2873a1b9be0f2846df97b0a53", "source_type": "x_thread", "status": "evidenced", "summary_hint": null, "title": "matt palmer - Getting Started with Grok Bot  01:00 What is @Bot? 05:26 Anatomy of a...", "topic": "Productivity and Workflows", "truncated": true, "truncation": {"byte_budget": true, "fields": ["hint"], "selection": true}, "url": "https://x.com/mattyp/status/2092286281266962681", "video_id": "2090953710696329216", "yoinked_at": "2026-08-26T07:57:42"}
